   "claims": [
    "GCF Calculator – Greatest Common Factor #1 #2 #3 Enter at least 2 numbers to calculate the GCF.",
    "Let's repeat the Euclidean algorithm for our examples using modulo instead of ordinary subtraction: GCF of 72 and 40: 72 mod 40 = 32, GCF of 40 and 32: 40 mod 32 = 8, GCF of 32 and 8: 32 mod 8 = 0 STOP!",
    "GCF of 35,640 and 33,264: 35,640 mod 33,264 = 2376, GCF of 33,264 and 2376: 33,264 mod 2376 = 0 STOP!",
    "Two even numbers: gcf(35,640, 33,264) = 2 × gcf(17,820, 16,632) = 2² × gcf(8910, 8316) = 2³ × gcf(4455, 4158) = ….",
    "One even one odd: … = 2³ × gcf(4455, 2079).",
    "Two odd: … = 2³ × gcf((4455-2079)/2, 2079) = 2³ × gcf(1188, 2079).",
    "One even one odd: … = 2³ × gcf(594, 2079) = 2³ × gcf(297, 2079).",
    "Two odd: … = 2³ × gcf((2079-297)/2, 297) = 2³ × gcf(891, 297).",
    "Two odd: … = 2³ × gcf((891-297)/2, 297) = 2³ × gcf(297, 297) = 2³ × 297 = 2376.",
    "In other words, we can write that numbers A and B are coprime if gcf(A,B) = 1."
   ],
